{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543544-the-addams-family-as-outcasts","id":1543544,"title":"The Addams Family as Outcasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-10T14:35:15-07:00","id":1543544,"title":"The Addams Family as Outcasts","content":"Not literally the Addams family, but something like them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve long liked the idea of a dark twisted sort of family, like the Addams family but played seriously. Kind of like Revenant families from V:tM as well, but without the vampire masters. It seemed to me that Outcasts, which could be people carrying the blood of demons, might be a good way to pull off the dark Addams and /or Revenant family sort of feel.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure if I could fit that idea into one of the current Outcast families. None quite match up. The Nephilim are a literal family, but their theme of roaming around acquiring knowledge isn\u2019t quite the one I\u2019m looking for. The twisted outcast among outcast aspects of the Chimera have a little of that theme I\u2019m thinking of, though they aren\u2019t a family. The Keepers of the Broken Vine could maybe pull off a more rural sort of variation on this idea, but once again, not really a family.<br /> <br /> Does anybody have any ideas about incorporating this kind of concept into the Outcasts? Maybe as a tweak of one of the existing families, a noteworthy subgroup of another family, or their own family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T01:58:07-07:00","id":1543575,"title":"","content":"<b>Remember - Curseborne is coming from <i>CoD</i>-like gameline model</b> - There is no 'hard canon' like in <b>WoD</b>, it almost from basis assumes people are homebrewing stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Like popular saying goes - 'devs police will not come to your table and lock you for making your own stuff'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543544-the-addams-family-as-outcasts#post1543544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The twisted outcast among outcast aspects of the Chimera have a little of that theme I\u2019m thinking of, though they aren\u2019t a family. The Keepers of the Broken Vine could maybe pull off a more rural sort of variation on this idea, but once again, not really a family.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could just use Chimera or Broken Vine Families and make their local chapter... well, family. This local group is just blood-related, even in at global, Family is more 'chosen family'.<br /> <br /> Also, you can simply make your own particular Family by homebrew - we have enough mechanics for those Paths from example to make things yourself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T12:10:21-07:00","id":1543627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543544-the-addams-family-as-outcasts#post1543544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The twisted outcast among outcast aspects of the Chimera have a little of that theme I\u2019m thinking of, though they aren\u2019t a family. The Keepers of the Broken Vine could maybe pull off a more rural sort of variation on this idea, but once again, not really a family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit confused as to why you think these two aren't families, especially the Chimera. Outcast traits seem to be purely inherited. You could probably join the KOTBVs but Chimera are highly specific and it feels like the only way you get to be one is by being born that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:35:29-07:00","id":1543658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1543544-the-addams-family-as-outcasts?p=1543627#post1543627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a bit confused as to why you think these two aren't families, especially the Chimera. Outcast traits seem to be purely inherited. You could probably join the KOTBVs but Chimera are highly specific and it feels like the only way you get to be one is by being born that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Upon rereading, you\u2019re right about the Chimera. While the description doesn\u2019t focus on the family nature of them, it does make it pretty clear that their condition is hereditary and portraying them as a literal family dies follow pretty naturally. The more I think about it, maybe the Chimera are potentially what I\u2019m looking for. <br /> <br /> In the case of the Keepers of the Broken Vine, the door is open for a strong hereditary component, but the flavor text emphasizes that any are welcome to join them and their sample character\u2019s opinion on the Nephilim is highly critical of their focus on family, calling it bigotry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:49:42-07:00","id":1543661,"title":"","content":"I guess my default take for all Families is that they're literal families on some level unless stated otherwise. The Keepers being open to outsiders and no liking the Nephilim attitude doesn't mean that they don't also by default bring their kids up in their belief system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}